1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,700
Meet deprehendo.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:10,700
When a self-hosted GitHub Actions runner dies in the
middle of a job, deprehendo tells you why.

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:16,700
Getting started takes three commands: build the
agent, log in, and upload.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:23,200
Every incident your organization uploads lands here,
newest first.

5
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:31,200
Open one, and the diagnosis is right at the top.
Here, an out-of-memory kill, with high confidence.

6
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:39,200
Click any piece of evidence to see its source, its
timing, and the raw value, exactly as recorded.

7
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:47,200
The causal chain and timeline show what was observed
directly, and what was inferred.

8
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:55,200
And when nothing matches, it says so, and shows what
GitHub itself reported.

9
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:02,200
Light or dark. Compact or comfortable. In your own
time zone.

10
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,200
deprehendo. Every conclusion, inspectable.
